   <section id="content-guidelines">
        <h2>Content Guidelines</h2>
        <div class="section-content">
            <h3>Writing Style</h3>
            <p>Write in a clear, concise, and engaging style. Use active voice and avoid jargon. Maintain a friendly and approachable tone, reflecting the African Bank brand personality. Prioritize clarity and accuracy in all communications.</p>
            <h3>Content Formats</h3>
            <p>
              <b>Website Copy:</b> Website copy should be informative, persuasive, and easy to scan. Use headings, subheadings, bullet points, and short paragraphs to break up text and improve readability. Optimize content for search engines (SEO) using relevant keywords. <br><br>
              <b>Blog Posts:</b> Blog posts provide an opportunity to share valuable insights and engage with your audience. Use a conversational tone and incorporate storytelling elements. Include visuals and calls to action.<br><br>
              <b>Social Media:</b> Social media content should be concise, engaging, and tailored to the specific platform. Use strong visuals and relevant hashtags. Encourage interaction and respond promptly to comments and messages. <br><br>
              <b>Email Marketing:</b> Email marketing should be personalized and targeted. Use compelling subject lines and clear calls to action. Ensure emails are mobile-friendly. 
            </p>
            <h3>Accessibility</h3>
            <p>
              <b>Alt Text for Images:</b> Provide descriptive alt text for all images. This is essential for users with visual impairments and also benefits search engine optimization.<br><br>
              <b>Captions for Videos:</b> Provide captions for all videos to make them accessible to users who are deaf or hard of hearing.<br><br>
              <b>Keyboard Navigation:</b> Ensure that all interactive elements can be accessed and used using a keyboard.<br><br>
              <b>Color Contrast:</b> Maintain sufficient color contrast between text and background colors to ensure readability for users with low vision.<br><br>
              <b>ARIA Attributes:</b> Use ARIA attributes where necessary to improve accessibility for screen readers.
            </p>
            <h3>Grammar and Punctuation</h3>
            <p>Adhere to standard English grammar and punctuation rules. Maintain consistency in style and usage.</p>
            <h3>Legal Considerations</h3>
            <p>Ensure all content complies with relevant legal regulations and guidelines. Avoid making unsubstantiated claims or using copyrighted material without permission.</p>

        </div>
    </section>

